---
import StarlightLayout from '~/layouts/StarlightLayout.astro';
import MetricsSection from '~/components/home/MetricsSection.astro';

const TITLE = 'About Distr';
const DESCRIPTION =
  'Distr is an open-source software distribution platform for vendors who ship their software into customer-controlled environments.';

const ldJson = (obj: unknown) => JSON.stringify(obj).replace(/</g, '\\u003c');

const head = [
  {
    tag: 'script' as const,
    attrs: {type: 'application/ld+json'},
    content: ldJson({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'Organization',
      name: 'Glasskube',
      url: 'https://distr.sh',
      brand: {'@type': 'Brand', name: 'Distr'},
      address: [
        {
          '@type': 'PostalAddress',
          addressLocality: 'Vienna',
          addressCountry: 'AT',
        },
        {
          '@type': 'PostalAddress',
          addressLocality: 'Chicago',
          addressCountry: 'US',
        },
      ],
      sameAs: [
        'https://github.com/distr-sh/distr',
        'https://linkedin.com/company/glasskube',
        'https://x.com/glasskube',
        'https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/glasskube',
      ],
    }),
  },
];

const link =
  'text-accent-600 underline hover:text-accent-900 dark:text-accent-300 dark:hover:text-accent-200';
---

<StarlightLayout title={TITLE} description={DESCRIPTION} head={head}>
  <div class="not-content about-page">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold my-8">{TITLE}</h1>

      <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        {DESCRIPTION} It delivers Docker Compose and Helm applications from one platform,
        with guided installation, customer entitlements, offline license keys, logs
        and metrics.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-10">
        Distr is built by Glasskube, a company backed by Y Combinator and based
        in Vienna, Austria and Chicago, US. The platform and both deployment
        agents are open source under the Apache 2.0 license on <a
          href="https://github.com/distr-sh/distr"
          class={link}>GitHub</a
        >.
      </p>
    </article>

    <MetricsSection />

    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Why we built Distr</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        We started with an open-source package manager for Kubernetes that grew
        to nearly 3,500 GitHub stars. Soon, startups in our network asked for
        help getting their applications into large enterprise environments, so
        we spent a long time writing Helm charts and containerizing applications
        for them.
      </p>

      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        We learned quickly that a Helm chart or a Compose file is a great start,
        but not enough to ship software reliably. The hard part comes after the
        first install: maintaining, observing, updating and securing every
        customer environment over time. Solving that is why we built Distr.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">What we believe</h2>

      <ul
        class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        <li>Keep it as simple as possible, both for you and your customers.</li>
        <li>
          A distribution platform should be open source and self-hostable.
        </li>
        <li>
          Every enterprise environment is different, so the platform needs to be
          as flexible as possible.
        </li>
        <li>
          Application design matters: architecting for a self-hostable product
          is half the struggle.
        </li>
        <li>Standards over lock-in.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Who uses Distr</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        Teams at Artifact, Basedash, Lerian, Ozgar AI, Sophris.ai and Weave use
        Distr to ship their software to self-hosted customers. Read how in our <a
          href="/case-studies/"
          class={link}>case studies</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4">Get involved</h2>

      <p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6">
        Distr is developed in the open. Browse the code, open an issue or join
        the discussion on <a
          href="https://github.com/distr-sh/distr/discussions"
          class={link}>GitHub</a
        >. For anything else, <a href="/contact/" class={link}>get in touch</a> with
        our team.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</StarlightLayout>

<style>
  .not-content {
    max-width: none;
  }
  .about-page article {
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }
</style>
